IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wills-dates`

-- Wills Act 2000 (NT) -- the rules a will-maker, and a person with an interest in a deceased person's will, meet: what
-- may be left by will (s 6), who may make a will (ss 3, 7, 18), executing and witnessing it (ss 8, 9, 11, 12), revoking,
-- altering and reviving it (ss 13-17), Court-authorised wills for persons without testamentary capacity (ss 19, 21, 25),
-- informal wills (s 10), rectification and its time limit (s 27), what becomes of a gift to a beneficiary who dies before
-- or soon after the will-maker (ss 30, 34, 40, 41(2)), wills made under another law and international wills (s 46, Part 5A
-- and the Annex), depositing a will and getting it back (ss 50, 51), who may see a will (s 54), and a maintenance
-- distribution in the first 30 days (s 55).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in wills-seat.l4 (the will-maker) and wills-seat-family.l4 (the
-- person with an interest in a deceased person's will), which IMPORT it and never restate a rule. Nothing here is
-- exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("is not valid", "is not valid
-- unless", "is not effective unless", "may be revoked but only", "may not", "is void", "must refuse leave ... unless",
-- "must not make an order unless", "does not apply", an "if" condition that fails, a period the text fixes); or NOTHING where
-- the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The Court's judgments ("satisfied", "thinks it
-- is just") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them. Forks (Fn) are listed in NOTES.md.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word reprint REPW007 of the Wills Act
-- 2000 (NT), as in force at 1 January 2022, not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned
-- by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October
-- 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Wills Act 2000 (NT) -- the rules for the will-maker and the family`

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions (s 3)`

-- s 3: "minor means a person who is less than 18 years of age."
GIVEN `the age in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a minor` `the age in years` IF `the age in years` LESS THAN 18

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 -- what may be left by will (s 6)`

DECLARE `My hold on the property at my death` IS ONE OF
    `I am entitled to it at my death`
    `my personal representative becomes entitled to it, as personal representative, after my death`
    `I hold it as trustee at my death`
    `none of these`

-- s 6(1): "A person may dispose by will of property to which the person is entitled at the time of his or her death."
-- (2): "... property to which the personal representative of that person becomes entitled by virtue of the office of
-- personal representative after the death of that person." (3): whether or not the entitlement exists when the will is
-- made. (4): "A person may not dispose by will of property of which the person is trustee at the time of his or her
-- death." (4) is a flat negative: JUST FALSE. Outside the three heads the Act is silent: NOTHING.
GIVEN `my hold` IS A `My hold on the property at my death`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 -- I may leave this property by my will` `my hold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my hold`
    WHEN `I am entitled to it at my death` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `my personal representative becomes entitled to it, as personal representative, after my death` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `I hold it as trustee at my death` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `none of these` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 6 grants two heads and forbids one; it does not close the list)

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 and Part 3 Division 1 -- who may make a will (ss 7, 18)`

DECLARE `Marital status` IS ONE OF
    `never married`
    `married now`
    `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)`

DECLARE `Whether my will is valid as to my age` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am 18 or over`
    `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under Part 3`
    `yes: I am a married minor (s 7(2)(b))`
    `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 7(2)(a))`
    `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 7(1))`

-- s 7(1): "Subject to subsection (2) and Part 3, a will made by a minor is not valid." (2): "A minor: (a) may make a will
-- in contemplation of marriage (and may alter or revoke the will) but the will is of no effect if the marriage
-- contemplated does not take place; (b) if he or she is married - may make, alter or revoke a will; and (c) if he or she has
-- been married - may revoke the whole or any part of a will made while the minor was married or in contemplation of his or
-- her marriage." Part 3: s 18(1) (a minor's will by Court order) and s 19(4) (an order for a minor without testamentary
-- capacity). The age is the age when the will is made. Testamentary capacity (soundness of mind) is common law: out.
GIVEN `my age when I make it` IS A NUMBER
      `my marital status` IS A `Marital status`
      `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has authorised it by order under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my will is valid as to my age`
`ss 7, 18 -- my will is valid as to my age` `my age when I make it` `my marital status` `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` `the Court has authorised it by order under Part 3` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age when I make it` THEN `yes: I am 18 or over`
           IF `the Court has authorised it by order under Part 3` THEN `yes: the Court authorised it by an order under Part 3`
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married now` THEN `yes: I am a married minor (s 7(2)(b))`
           IF `I make it in contemplation of a marriage` THEN `yes, but it has no effect if the marriage I contemplate does not take place (s 7(2)(a))`
           OTHERWISE `no: a will made by a minor is not valid (s 7(1))`

-- Revoking as a minor: s 7(2)(a), (b), (c) and s 18(1)(b). s 7(1) speaks only of a will "made" by a minor; for any other
-- minor the Act is silent on revoking (fork F1).
GIVEN `my age now` IS A NUMBER
      `my marital status` IS A `Marital status`
      `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made while I was married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 7, 18 -- I may revoke my will although a minor` `my age now` `my marital status` `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` `the will was made while I was married` `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under Part 3` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age now` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the Court has authorised the revocation by order under Part 3` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married now` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the will was made in contemplation of a marriage` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `my marital status` EQUALS `married before, but not now (divorced or widowed)` AND `the will was made while I was married` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 7(1) invalidates a will made by a minor, it does not speak of revoking; s 7(2) grants revocation to the minors it names; fork F1)

-- s 18(2): "Before making the order the Court must be satisfied that: (a) the minor understands the nature and effect of
-- the proposed will or alteration or revocation of the will and the extent of the property disposed of by it; (b) the
-- proposed will or alteration or revocation of the will accurately reflects the intentions of the minor; and (c) it is
-- reasonable in all the circumstances that the order should be made." "must be satisfied" before the order: when any limb is
-- not met, JUST FALSE. For a person of 18 or over s 18 has nothing to do (a scope limit: NOTHING).
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(2) -- the Court may authorise my will as a minor` `my age` `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property` `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions` `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 3 -- a minor` `my age`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 18 speaks only of a minor; an adult needs no order)
    ELSE IF     `the Court is satisfied I understand the will and the property`
            AND `the Court is satisfied it accurately reflects my intentions`
            AND `the Court is satisfied the order is reasonable in all the circumstances`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 18(4): "A will or an instrument made pursuant to an order made under subsection (1) ... is not valid unless: (a) it is
-- executed as required by this Act; (b) one of the attesting witnesses is the Registrar; and (c) it is made in accordance
-- with the conditions of the order." "is not valid unless": JUST FALSE when any limb fails.
GIVEN `it is executed as the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is one of the attesting witnesses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it follows the conditions of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18(4) -- my Court-authorised will as a minor is valid` `it is executed as the Act requires` `the Registrar is one of the attesting witnesses` `it follows the conditions of the order` MEANS
    IF `it is executed as the Act requires` AND `the Registrar is one of the attesting witnesses` AND `it follows the conditions of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Division 2 -- executing and witnessing a will (ss 8, 9, 10, 11, 12)`

DECLARE `Who signed the will` IS ONE OF
    `I signed it myself`
    `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction`
    `someone else signed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction`
    `nobody signed it`

-- s 8(1): "A will is not valid unless: (a) it is in writing and signed by the testator or by some other person in the
-- presence of and at the direction of the testator; (b) the signature is made or acknowledged by the testator in the
-- presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time; and (c) at least 2 of those witnesses attest and sign the will
-- in the presence of the testator." (2): not necessarily in each other's presence. (3): the signature "(a) must be made with
-- the intention of executing the will; and (b) is not required to be made at the foot of the will." (4): no attestation
-- clause needed. s 9: a witness need not know it is a will. s 11: "A person who is not able to see and attest that a
-- testator has signed a document may not be a witness to a will." So only witnesses able to see count (fork F2). "is not
-- valid unless": JUST FALSE when any limb fails. "document" (s 3): paper or other material with writing on it.
GIVEN `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who signed` IS A `Who signed the will`
      `signed intending to execute the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` IS A NUMBER
      `of them, how many then attested and signed the will in my presence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 8, 11 -- my will is validly executed` `it is in writing` `who signed` `signed intending to execute the will` `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` `of them, how many then attested and signed the will in my presence` MEANS
    IF     `it is in writing`
       AND `the signature is a proper one`
       AND `signed intending to execute the will`
       AND `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature` AT LEAST 2
       AND `the attesting witnesses` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the signature is a proper one` MEANS
            CONSIDER `who signed`
            WHEN `I signed it myself` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `someone else signed it, in my presence and at my direction` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `the attesting witnesses` MEANS
            IF `of them, how many then attested and signed the will in my presence` GREATER THAN `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature`
            THEN `witnesses able to see, present together when I signed or acknowledged my signature`
            ELSE `of them, how many then attested and signed the will in my presence`

DECLARE `What becomes of a gift to a witness` IS ONE OF
    `s 12 does not touch it: the beneficiary was not a witness`
    `not void: at least 2 of the witnesses take nothing under the will (s 12(2)(a))`
    `not void: everyone who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing (s 12(2)(b))`
    `not void: the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of it and gave it freely (s 12(2)(c))`
    `void, as far as it concerns the witness and anyone claiming under them (s 12(1))`

-- s 12(1): "Subject to subsection (2), if a beneficial disposition is given or made by will to a person who is a witness to
-- the will, the disposition is void to the extent that it concerns the person or a person claiming under him or her." (2):
-- "not void ... if: (a) at least 2 of the witnesses to the will are not persons to whom a beneficial disposition is given or
-- made by the will; (b) all the persons who would benefit directly from the avoidance of the disposition consent in writing
-- to the distribution of the disposition according to the will; or (c) the Court is satisfied that: (i) the testator knew
-- and approved of the disposition; and (ii) the disposition was given or made freely and voluntarily by the testator." s 12
-- does not reach a witness's spouse or partner (finding 3).
GIVEN `the beneficiary witnessed the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `witnesses who take nothing under the will` IS A NUMBER
      `all who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of the gift` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the gift was made freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of a gift to a witness`
`s 12 -- what becomes of a gift to a witness` `the beneficiary witnessed the will` `witnesses who take nothing under the will` `all who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing` `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of the gift` `the Court is satisfied the gift was made freely and voluntarily` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the beneficiary witnessed the will` THEN `s 12 does not touch it: the beneficiary was not a witness`
           IF `witnesses who take nothing under the will` AT LEAST 2 THEN `not void: at least 2 of the witnesses take nothing under the will (s 12(2)(a))`
           IF `all who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing` THEN `not void: everyone who would gain from its avoidance consented in writing (s 12(2)(b))`
           IF `the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of the gift` AND `the Court is satisfied the gift was made freely and voluntarily` THEN `not void: the Court is satisfied the will-maker knew and approved of it and gave it freely (s 12(2)(c))`
           OTHERWISE `void, as far as it concerns the witness and anyone claiming under them (s 12(1))`

-- s 10(2): "If the Court is satisfied that a deceased person intended a document or part of a document that purports to
-- embody the testamentary intentions of the deceased person (but which is not executed in the manner required by this Act)
-- to constitute his or her will or an alteration of his or her will or to revoke his or her will, the document ...
-- constitutes the will ... or an alteration of the will or revokes the will, as the case requires." (1): "document" here is
-- wide (marks, sounds, images, a map or photograph). (4): made in or outside the Territory. An "if" condition: JUST FALSE
-- when the Court is not satisfied, or the document does not purport to embody testamentary intentions. A document that
-- was properly executed does not need s 10 (a scope limit: NOTHING).
GIVEN `the document was executed as the Act requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended it as their will, alteration or revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 -- the Court may accept the document as the will` `the document was executed as the Act requires` `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions` `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended it as their will, alteration or revocation` MEANS
    IF `the document was executed as the Act requires`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 10 reaches a document "not executed in the manner required by this Act")
    ELSE IF `the document purports to embody the deceased's testamentary intentions` AND `the Court is satisfied the deceased intended it as their will, alteration or revocation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 2 Division 3 -- revoking, altering and reviving a will (ss 13-17)`

DECLARE `What was done to the will` IS ONE OF
    `I made a later will that revokes it`
    `I signed a writing declaring I revoke it, executed like a will`
    `I burned, tore or destroyed it, intending to revoke it`
    `someone else destroyed it in my presence, at my direction, with my intention to revoke it`
    `someone else destroyed it, but not in my presence or not at my direction`
    `it was destroyed by accident or without an intention to revoke it`
    `I wrote on it or dealt with it so that the Court is satisfied from its state that I intended to revoke it`
    `the Court ordered it revoked under Part 3`
    `I said or wrote that I revoke it, without executing the writing like a will`
    `I made a later will that does not revoke it`

-- s 13: "The whole or a part of a will may be revoked but only: (a) in the circumstances in respect of revoking a will
-- specified in Division 1 or 2 of Part 3; (b) by the operation of section 14 or 15; (c) by a later will; (d) by some writing
-- declaring an intention to revoke the will, executed in the manner in which a will is required to be executed by this Act;
-- (e) by the testator, or another person in the testator's presence and at the testator's direction, burning, tearing or
-- otherwise destroying the will with the intention of the testator of revoking it; or (f) by the testator, or another
-- person in the testator's presence and at the testator's direction, writing on the will or dealing with the will in such a
-- manner that the Court is satisfied from the state of the will that the testator intended to revoke it." "but only" closes
-- the list: JUST FALSE outside it. Whether a later will revokes an earlier one (an express clause, or inconsistency) is
-- common law, asked as a choice (fork F3). Marriage and divorce (s 13(b)) are their own questions. A writing that misses
-- the formalities may still be admitted by the Court under s 10 after death.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What was done to the will`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- my will is revoked by what was done` `what was done` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what was done`
    WHEN `I made a later will that revokes it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `I signed a writing declaring I revoke it, executed like a will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `I burned, tore or destroyed it, intending to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `someone else destroyed it in my presence, at my direction, with my intention to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `I wrote on it or dealt with it so that the Court is satisfied from its state that I intended to revoke it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Court ordered it revoked under Part 3` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `What my marriage does to my will` IS ONE OF
    `s 14 does not arise: I have not married since I made the will`
    `not revoked: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 14(3))`
    `not revoked: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 14(4))`
    `revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death (s 14(1), (2))`

-- s 14(1): "Subject to this section, a will is revoked by the marriage of the testator." (2): the marriage does not revoke
-- "(a) a disposition to the person to whom the testator is married at the time of his or her death; (b) an appointment as
-- executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian of the person to whom the testator is married at the time of his or her
-- death; and (c) a will made in exercise of a power of appointment" where the property would not otherwise pass to the
-- executor, administrator or the Public Trustee. (3): "A will made in contemplation of a marriage, whether or not that
-- contemplation is expressed in the will, is not revoked by the solemnisation of that marriage." (4): "A will that is
-- expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally is not revoked by the solemnisation of a marriage of the
-- testator." Only marriage: a de facto relationship does not revoke (finding 2).
GIVEN `I have married since I made the will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What my marriage does to my will`
`s 14 -- what my marriage does to my will` `I have married since I made the will` `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage` `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I have married since I made the will` THEN `s 14 does not arise: I have not married since I made the will`
           IF `the will was made in contemplation of that marriage` THEN `not revoked: the will was made in contemplation of this marriage (s 14(3))`
           IF `the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally` THEN `not revoked: the will is expressed to be made in contemplation of marriage generally (s 14(4))`
           OTHERWISE `revoked, except gifts to and appointments of the person I am married to at my death (s 14(1), (2))`

DECLARE `How the marriage ended` IS ONE OF
    `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975`
    `a decree of nullity was granted by the Family Court`
    `dissolved or annulled outside Australia, and recognised in Australia under the Family Law Act 1975`
    `dissolved or annulled outside Australia, but not recognised in Australia`
    `we separated, but the marriage has not been dissolved or annulled`

DECLARE `Part of my will about my former spouse` IS ONE OF
    `a gift to my former spouse`
    `my former spouse's appointment as executor, guardian or advisory trustee`
    `my former spouse's appointment as trustee of property left on trust for beneficiaries who include my former spouse's children`
    `my former spouse's appointment as trustee of other property`
    `a power of appointment my former spouse may exercise only in favour of our children`
    `another power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of my former spouse`
    `a part that does not concern my former spouse`

-- s 15(2): a marriage ends by divorce or annulment "(a) when a decree of dissolution of the testator's marriage becomes
-- absolute under the Family Law Act 1975 ...; (b) on the granting of a decree of nullity ... by the Family Court; or (c) on
-- the dissolution or annulment of the marriage in accordance with the law of a place outside Australia, but only if that
-- dissolution or annulment is recognised in Australia under the Family Law Act 1975". (3): divorce or annulment revokes
-- "(a) a beneficial disposition made by the testator to the testator's spouse in a will in existence at the time of the
-- divorce or annulment; (b) an appointment of the testator's spouse as an executor, trustee, advisory trustee or guardian
-- made by the will; and (c) a grant made by the will of a power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of the testator's
-- spouse." (4): "Subsection (3) does not apply if a contrary intention appears in the will or is otherwise established."
-- (5): it "does not revoke: (a) the appointment of the testator's spouse as trustee of property left on trust for
-- beneficiaries that include the spouse's children ...; or (b) the grant ... of a power of appointment exercisable by the
-- testator's spouse exclusively in favour of the children of whom both the testator and his or her spouse are the
-- parents." (6): the will takes effect as if the spouse had died before the testator. A marriage that has not ended in one
-- of the s 15(2) ways: JUST FALSE ("for the purposes of this section, a testator's marriage ends ... when", closed by "but
-- only"). (4) and (5) are flat negatives: JUST FALSE. A part not about the spouse: JUST FALSE, because s 13 closes the ways
-- a will is revoked. (a) is read as a divorce order taking effect (fork F4; finding 4). s 5(3): the divorce or annulment
-- must be after 1 March 2001 (assumed).
GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How the marriage ended`
      `the part` IS A `Part of my will about my former spouse`
      `a contrary intention appears in the will or is otherwise established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- my divorce revokes this part of my will` `how it ended` `the part` `a contrary intention appears in the will or is otherwise established` MEANS
    IF NOT `the marriage has ended under s 15(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears in the will or is otherwise established`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE CONSIDER `the part`
              WHEN `a gift to my former spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `my former spouse's appointment as executor, guardian or advisory trustee` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `my former spouse's appointment as trustee of other property` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `another power of appointment exercisable by or in favour of my former spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the marriage has ended under s 15(2)` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it ended`
            WHEN `a divorce order took effect under the Family Law Act 1975` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a decree of nullity was granted by the Family Court` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `dissolved or annulled outside Australia, and recognised in Australia under the Family Law Act 1975` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `How the change was made` IS ONE OF
    `signed by me and witnessed like a will (signatures may be in the margin or on a memorandum)`
    `made as a minor under a Court order under s 18(1), as the order requires`
    `made for me under a Court order under s 19(1), while I lacked testamentary capacity`
    `the Court is satisfied under s 10 that it embodies my intentions (after my death)`
    `I obliterated words so that their effect is no longer apparent`
    `none of these (for example, initialled by me only, or not witnessed)`

-- s 16(1): "An alteration made to a will after the will is executed is not effective unless the alteration: (a) is executed
-- in a manner in which a will is required to be executed by this Act; (b) is made by a minor pursuant to an order of the
-- Court made under section 18(1) ...; (c) is made for and on behalf of a person without testamentary capacity pursuant to an
-- order ... under section 19(1) ...; (d) is a document that under section 10 the Court is satisfied embodies testamentary
-- intentions ...; or (e) obliterates words in the will so that their effect is no longer apparent." (2): the signatures may
-- be in the margin or authenticate a memorandum. (3): "This section does not apply to an alteration to a will if the words or
-- effect of the will are no longer apparent because of the alteration." (1)(e) and (3) speak of the same alteration (finding
-- 1): an obliteration answers NOTHING (fork F5). An alteration made before the will was executed is outside s 16 (a scope
-- limit: NOTHING). "is not effective unless": JUST FALSE for an alteration that meets none of (a)-(e).
GIVEN `the change was made after the will was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how it was made` IS A `How the change was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- my change to my will is effective` `the change was made after the will was executed` `how it was made` MEANS
    IF NOT `the change was made after the will was executed`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 16(1) speaks of an alteration made "after the will is executed")
    ELSE CONSIDER `how it was made`
         WHEN `I obliterated words so that their effect is no longer apparent` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (s 16(1)(e) lists it, s 16(3) disapplies the section to it; fork F5)
         WHEN `none of these (for example, initialled by me only, or not witnessed)` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `How I tried to revive it` IS ONE OF
    `I re-executed the revoked will`
    `I executed a will showing an intention to revive it`
    `something else (for example, I taped the torn will together, or I said it should stand)`

-- s 17(1): "A will or a part of a will that has been revoked is revived by re-execution or by execution of a will showing an
-- intention to revive the will or part." (2): a revived will is taken to have been executed on the date it is revived. (3),
-- (4): reviving a will that was revoked in stages revives only the part most recently revoked, unless the reviving will shows
-- a contrary intention. Not closed with "only": another way answers NOTHING.
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I tried to revive it`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 -- my revoked will is revived` `how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `something else (for example, I taped the torn will together, or I said it should stand)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 17(1) names two ways and does not close the list)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- a Court-authorised will for a person without testamentary capacity (ss 19, 21, 25)`

-- s 19(3): "The Court must not make an order under this Division unless the person in respect of whom the application is
-- made is alive when the order is made." s 20(1): leave of the Court is needed first. s 21: "The Court must refuse leave ...
-- unless the Court is satisfied that: (a) there is reason to believe that the proposed testator is or may be incapable of
-- making a will; (b) the proposed will or alteration or revocation of a will is or might be one that would have been made by
-- the proposed testator if he or she had testamentary capacity; (c) it is or may be appropriate for an order ... to be
-- made ...; (d) the applicant is an appropriate person to make the application; and (e) adequate steps have been taken to
-- allow representation of all persons with a legitimate interest ...". The answer is whether the Court MAY grant leave; it is
-- never obliged to (s 22). "must refuse ... unless" and "must not ... unless": JUST FALSE when any limb fails. s 19(3) is
-- about the order; leave for a person already dead would be pointless, so the two are taken together (fork F9).
GIVEN `my relative is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reason to believe they are or may be incapable of making a will` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposed will is or might be one they would have made with capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is or may be appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an appropriate person to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adequate steps taken to let everyone with a legitimate interest be represented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 19(3), 21 -- the Court may give leave for a will for my relative` `my relative is alive` `reason to believe they are or may be incapable of making a will` `the proposed will is or might be one they would have made with capacity` `an order is or may be appropriate` `I am an appropriate person to apply` `adequate steps taken to let everyone with a legitimate interest be represented` MEANS
    IF     `my relative is alive`
       AND `reason to believe they are or may be incapable of making a will`
       AND `the proposed will is or might be one they would have made with capacity`
       AND `an order is or may be appropriate`
       AND `I am an appropriate person to apply`
       AND `adequate steps taken to let everyone with a legitimate interest be represented`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 25(2): "Despite section 51, a will referred to in subsection (1) may not be withdrawn from deposit with the prescribed
-- person by or on behalf of the person on whose behalf it was made unless: (a) the Court makes an order under this Division
-- authorising the revocation of the will; or (b) the person acquires or regains testamentary capacity." s 51(1), (2): a
-- testator may apply in writing to be given a deposited will, and the prescribed person "must give the will ... unless the
-- testator is a minor or a person who lacks testamentary capacity". Both are "unless" negatives: JUST FALSE. Whether the
-- testator is a minor is worked out from the age (s 3).
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I have testamentary capacity now` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a will made for me by Court order while I lacked capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has authorised its revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I applied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 25(2), 51(1), (2) -- I can get my deposited will back` `my age` `I have testamentary capacity now` `it is a will made for me by Court order while I lacked capacity` `the Court has authorised its revocation` `I applied in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I applied in writing` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: the duty in s 51(2) follows an application "in writing" under s 51(1))
           IF `it is a will made for me by Court order while I lacked capacity` AND (NOT `I have testamentary capacity now`) AND `the Court has authorised its revocation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (s 25(2)(a) lifts the bar and s 25(3) has the prescribed person comply with the order, but s 51(2) still withholds the will from a testator who lacks capacity; fork F11)
           IF `it is a will made for me by Court order while I lacked capacity` AND (NOT `I have testamentary capacity now`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `s 3 -- a minor` `my age` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF NOT `I have testamentary capacity now` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- rectification and its time limit (s 27)`

DECLARE `Why the will does not carry out the will-maker's intentions` IS ONE OF
    `a clerical error was made`
    `the will does not give effect to the will-maker's instructions`
    `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)`

-- s 27(1): "If the Court is satisfied that a will does not carry out the intentions of the testator because: (a) a clerical
-- error was made; or (b) the will does not give effect to the testator's instructions, the Court may make an order to
-- rectify the will so it carries out the testator's intentions." An "if" condition: JUST FALSE for another reason or when
-- the Court is not satisfied. JUST TRUE means the Court may rectify, not that it must.
GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Why the will does not carry out the will-maker's intentions`
      `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 27(1) -- the Court may rectify the will` `the reason` `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `some other reason (a change of mind, a mistake about the law or the effect of the words)` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Court is satisfied the will does not carry out the intentions for that reason` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 27(2): "A person who wishes to make an application for an order under this section must apply to the Court within 6
-- months after the date of the death of the testator." The last day: six calendar months after the death, the day of death
-- excluded (wills-dates.l4, fork F7). The duty is a regulative rule: DO apply WITHIN the days to that last day, counted from
-- the day of death (day 0), LEST BREACH. The "breach" is losing the right to apply without an extension, not a wrong.
-- (3): "The Court may ... extend the time ... if the Court thinks it is just." (4): "either before or after the 6 month
-- period ... expires but not if the final distribution of the estate has been made."
DECLARE `Rectification party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`
DECLARE `Rectification act` IS ONE OF `apply to the Court for rectification`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 27(2) -- the last day to apply for rectification` `the day of death` MEANS `the last day of` 6 `months after` `the day of death`

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 27(2) -- the days allowed to apply` `the day of death` MEANS
    `the days from` `the day of death` `to` (`s 27(2) -- the last day to apply for rectification` `the day of death`)

GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Rectification party` `Rectification act`
`s 27(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months after the death` `the day of death` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO `apply to the Court for rectification`
    WITHIN `s 27(2) -- the days allowed to apply` `the day of death`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no application within 6 months after the date of the death of the testator: rectification only if the Court extends the time, and never after the final distribution of the estate (s 27(2)-(4))"

-- The helper that runs the rule over what happened. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not
-- BREACH: where the application was made, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks
-- whether applying today would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Rectification party` `Rectification act`
      `the time it was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is in time under` `the rule` `at` `the time it was made` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was made`), (EVENT `the applicant` `apply to the Court for rectification` `the time it was made`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my rectification application stands` IS ONE OF
    `made in time (s 27(2))`
    `still open: I can apply in time`
    `out of time, but the Court has extended the time (s 27(3))`
    `out of time: I need the Court to extend the time (s 27(3))`
    `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 27(4))`

-- Where the Court has extended the time, the answer is "extended" whatever the distribution input (fork F10).
GIVEN `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
      `the Court has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the estate has been finally distributed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where my rectification application stands`
`s 27(2)-(4) -- where my rectification application stands` `the day of death` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` `the Court has extended the time` `the estate has been finally distributed` MEANS
    IF `the application is in time under` (`s 27(2) -- apply for rectification within 6 months after the death` `the day of death`) `at` `the time`
    THEN IF `I have applied` THEN `made in time (s 27(2))` ELSE `still open: I can apply in time`
    ELSE BRANCH IF `the Court has extended the time` THEN `out of time, but the Court has extended the time (s 27(3))`
                IF `the estate has been finally distributed` THEN `out of time, and the Court cannot extend it: the estate has been finally distributed (s 27(4))`
                OTHERWISE `out of time: I need the Court to extend the time (s 27(3))`
    WHERE
        `the time` MEANS
            IF `I have applied`
            THEN `the days from` `the day of death` `to` `the day I applied`
            ELSE `the days from` `the day of death` `to` `today`

§§ `Part 4 -- what becomes of a gift to a beneficiary who dies before, or soon after, the will-maker (ss 30, 34, 40, 41)`

-- s 34(1): "If a testator makes a disposition to a person who dies within 30 days after the death of the testator, the
-- testator's will is to take effect as if the person had died immediately before the testator." (2): not "if a contrary
-- intention appears in the will"; (3): "a general requirement or condition that a beneficiary survive the testator does not
-- indicate a contrary intention". Counting: the day of the will-maker's death excluded; a beneficiary who dies on the 30th
-- day after has died "within 30 days" and has not survived "for 30 days" (s 40(1)(d)); one who dies on the 31st day has
-- (fork F6). A beneficiary who died before the will-maker (a negative count) has not survived either.
GIVEN `the will-maker's death` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary's death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` IF
    `the days from` `the will-maker's death` `to` `the beneficiary's death` AT MOST 30

DECLARE `What becomes of the gift` IS ONE OF
    `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
    `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 30(2), 34(2), 40(3), 41(3))`
    `held on trust for the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days (s 40(1))`
    `the failed part passes to the other fractional parts proportionately (s 41(2))`
    `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 30(1))`
    `the Act does not say: a failed gift of the residue itself (intestacy law decides)`

-- s 40(1): "Subject to this section, if: (a) a person makes a disposition to an issue of the person; (b) the disposition is
-- not a disposition to which section 38 applies; (c) the interest in property disposed is not determinable at or before the
-- death of the issue; and (d) the issue does not survive the testator for 30 days, the disposition is to be held on trust
-- for the issue of the first-mentioned issue who survive the testator for 30 days in the shares they would have taken of the
-- residuary estate of the first-mentioned issue if the first-mentioned issue had died intestate leaving only issue
-- surviving." (3): a contrary intention displaces it; (4) a general survival or age condition, or a joint tenancy alone, is
-- not one; (5): "If a condition is imposed on an original beneficiary and the beneficiary fails to survive the testator for
-- 30 days, the issue of the beneficiary may not take under this section unless the original beneficiary fulfilled the
-- condition." s 41(2): "If a part of a disposition in fractional parts of the whole or the residue of the estate of a testator
-- fails, that part passes to the part that does not fail and, if there is more than one part that does not fail, to all
-- those parts proportionately." s 30(1): a disposition (other than by exercise of a power of appointment) that is ineffective
-- falls into the residuary estate. One contrary-intention input stands for ss 30(2), 34(2), 40(3), 41(3) (fork F8). Where
-- the failed gift is a non-fractional gift of the residue itself, s 30 has nowhere to send it: a "does not say" constructor.
GIVEN `the beneficiary is still alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the will-maker's death` IS A DATE
      `the beneficiary's death` IS A DATE
      `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is to issue without limit of remoteness, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary had not fulfilled a condition the will imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is a fractional part of the whole or the residue of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is of the residue itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of the gift`
`ss 30, 34, 40, 41 -- what becomes of the gift` `the beneficiary is still alive` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue` `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days` `the gift is to issue without limit of remoteness, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death` `the beneficiary had not fulfilled a condition the will imposed` `the gift is a fractional part of the whole or the residue of the estate` `the gift is of the residue itself` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the beneficiary is still alive` THEN `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
           IF NOT `ss 34, 40 -- the beneficiary did not survive the will-maker by 30 days` `the will-maker's death` `the beneficiary's death` THEN `the gift takes effect: the beneficiary survived the will-maker by 30 days`
           IF `the will shows a contrary intention, beyond a general condition to survive` THEN `the will's own terms decide: it shows a contrary intention (ss 30(2), 34(2), 40(3), 41(3))`
           IF     `the beneficiary was the will-maker's child, grandchild or other issue`
              AND `the beneficiary's own issue survived the will-maker by 30 days`
              AND (NOT `the gift is to issue without limit of remoteness, or the interest ends at the beneficiary's death`)
              AND (NOT `the beneficiary had not fulfilled a condition the will imposed`)
              THEN `held on trust for the beneficiary's own issue who survive the will-maker by 30 days (s 40(1))`
           IF `the gift is a fractional part of the whole or the residue of the estate` THEN `the failed part passes to the other fractional parts proportionately (s 41(2))`
           IF `the gift is of the residue itself` THEN `the Act does not say: a failed gift of the residue itself (intestacy law decides)`
           OTHERWISE `the gift falls into the residuary estate (s 30(1))`

§§ `Part 5 and Part 5A -- wills made under another law, and international wills (s 46, ss 48B-48F, the Annex)`

-- s 46(1): "A will is properly executed if its execution conforms to the internal law in force in the place: (a) where it
-- was executed; (b) that was the testator's domicile or habitual residence either at the time the will was executed or at
-- the testator's death; or (c) of which the testator was a national either at the date of execution of the will or at the
-- testator's death." (2): a will made on a vessel or aircraft and the law of the place most closely connected with it.
-- Whether execution "conforms" to a foreign law is asked (borrowed). A grant ("is properly executed if"); when no head holds,
-- s 8 may still be met, so NOTHING (s 46 is not the only route).
GIVEN `conforms to the law where it was executed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conforms to the law of my nationality, when made or at death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made on a vessel or aircraft, conforming to the law of the place most closely connected with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 -- my will is properly executed under another place's law` `conforms to the law where it was executed` `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death` `conforms to the law of my nationality, when made or at death` `made on a vessel or aircraft, conforming to the law of the place most closely connected with it` MEANS
    IF    `conforms to the law where it was executed`
       OR `conforms to the law of my domicile or habitual residence, when made or at death`
       OR `conforms to the law of my nationality, when made or at death`
       OR `made on a vessel or aircraft, conforming to the law of the place most closely connected with it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 46 adds routes to formal validity; s 8 and s 10 remain)

DECLARE `The authorised person` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian legal practitioner acting in Australia`
    `a public notary of an Australian jurisdiction, acting in Australia`
    `a person authorised under the law of another country that is party to the Convention`
    `nobody authorised`

-- s 48C(1): "The Annex to the Convention has the force of law in this jurisdiction." s 48D: who is authorised. Annex
-- Art 1(1): a will "shall be valid as regards form ... if it is made in the form of an international will complying with the
-- provisions set out in Articles 2 to 5". Art 2: not for a will of two or more persons in one instrument. Art 3: in writing,
-- any language, by any means. Art 4(1): "The testator shall declare in the presence of two witnesses and of a person
-- authorized to act in connection with international wills that the document is his will and that he knows the contents
-- thereof." Art 5(1): in their presence the testator signs or acknowledges the signature; (3): "The witnesses and the
-- authorized person shall there and then attest the will by signing in the presence of the testator." (Arts 6-10, the
-- placing of signatures, numbering, date and certificate, are not among Arts 2-5, and Art 13 says a missing certificate does
-- not affect formal validity; finding 6.) s 48E: the witnesses' qualifications are the Territory's (s 11). Art 1(2): failing
-- as an international will does not stop it being formally valid as another kind (s 8, s 46): a failure answers NOTHING.
-- Art 5(2) (a testator unable to sign) is not encoded.
GIVEN `it is one person's will alone` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised person` IS A `The authorised person`
      `witnesses present` IS A NUMBER
      `I declared before them that it is my will and I know its contents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I signed or acknowledged my signature in their presence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witnesses and the authorised person then signed in my presence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 5A, Annex Arts 1-5 -- my will is valid in form as an international will` `it is one person's will alone` `it is in writing` `the authorised person` `witnesses present` `I declared before them that it is my will and I know its contents` `I signed or acknowledged my signature in their presence` `the witnesses and the authorised person then signed in my presence` MEANS
    IF     `it is one person's will alone`
       AND `it is in writing`
       AND (NOT (`the authorised person` EQUALS `nobody authorised`))
       AND `witnesses present` AT LEAST 2
       AND `I declared before them that it is my will and I know its contents`
       AND `I signed or acknowledged my signature in their presence`
       AND `the witnesses and the authorised person then signed in my presence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (Art 1(2): failing as an international will does not affect formal validity as a will of another kind)

§§ `Part 6 -- depositing a will (s 50)`

DECLARE `Why the will is being deposited` IS ONE OF
    `I am depositing my own will`
    `a Court-authorised will under Part 3`
    `my lawyer has died, or has ceased or is about to cease practising law in the Territory`

-- s 50(2): "A will is not to be deposited with a prescribed person unless it is in a sealed envelope that has written on it:
-- (a) the testator's name and address (as they appear in the will); (b) the name and address ... of each executor ...; (c)
-- the date of the will; and (d) the name of the person depositing the will." "is not to be deposited unless": JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `sealed envelope marked with my name and address, each executor's, the will's date and the depositor's name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) -- my will may be deposited in this envelope` `sealed envelope marked with my name and address, each executor's, the will's date and the depositor's name` MEANS
    IF `sealed envelope marked with my name and address, each executor's, the will's date and the depositor's name` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 50(4): "A person depositing a will ... must pay the prescribed fee unless: (a) the will is deposited ... (i) under Part 3;
-- or (ii) because a lawyer has died or has ceased or is about to cease practising law in the Territory; or (b) the fee is
-- waived by the prescribed person in accordance with the Regulations." The fee and the waiver rules are in Regulations that
-- are not deposited: the amount is not given here. s 49(3): with no person prescribed, the Public Trustee. "unless" met:
-- JUST FALSE (no fee).
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why the will is being deposited`
      `the prescribed person has waived the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(4) -- I must pay the deposit fee` `why` `the prescribed person has waived the fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the prescribed person has waived the fee` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `why` EQUALS `I am depositing my own will` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 6 and Part 7 -- getting the deceased's will, and seeing it (ss 51(3), (4), 54)`

DECLARE `Who I am to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `an executor named in the will`
    `a person entitled to apply for letters of administration with the will annexed`
    `a person named or referred to in the will`
    `the deceased's surviving spouse`
    `the deceased's child, grandchild or other issue`
    `a parent or guardian of the deceased`
    `a person entitled to a share if the deceased had died without a will`
    `a creditor or other person with a claim against the estate`
    `a beneficiary of an earlier will of the deceased`
    `a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or entitled on intestacy`
    `the deceased's de facto partner, not named in the will and not entitled on intestacy`
    `someone else`

-- s 51(3): after the testator's death, "an executor named in the will or a person who is entitled to apply for letters of
-- administration with the will annexed may apply in writing to the prescribed person to be given the will." (4): the
-- prescribed person "must give the will". Others: limited by its own wording, NOTHING.
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(3), (4) -- I can have the deposited will given to me` `who I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `an executor named in the will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person entitled to apply for letters of administration with the will annexed` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 51(3) names the executor and a person entitled to letters with the will annexed)

-- s 54(2): "A person who has possession or control of a will of a deceased person must allow any one or more of the
-- following persons to inspect the will and make copies of the will at their own expense: (a) a person named or referred to
-- in the will, whether as a beneficiary or otherwise; (b) the surviving spouse or issue of the deceased person; (c) a parent
-- or a guardian of the deceased person; (d) a person who would be entitled to a share of the deceased person's estate if the
-- deceased person had died intestate; (e) a creditor or other person having a claim at law or in equity against the
-- deceased person's estate; (f) a beneficiary of a prior will of the deceased person; (g) a parent or guardian of a minor
-- referred to in the will or a minor who would be entitled to a share ... if the deceased person had died intestate." (1):
-- "will" includes a revoked will, a purported will, part of a will and a copy. The list is not closed with "only": outside
-- it, NOTHING. An executor named in the will is "named ... in the will" (a). A person entitled to letters with the will
-- annexed is not named as such: NOTHING unless also in the list. A de facto partner is not named (finding 5).
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Who I am to the deceased`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 -- I am entitled to inspect and copy the will` `who I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who I am`
    WHEN `an executor named in the will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person named or referred to in the will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the deceased's surviving spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the deceased's child, grandchild or other issue` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a parent or guardian of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person entitled to a share if the deceased had died without a will` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a creditor or other person with a claim against the estate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a beneficiary of an earlier will of the deceased` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a parent or guardian of a minor named in the will or entitled on intestacy` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (listed without closing the list)

§§ `Part 7 -- a maintenance distribution in the first 30 days (s 55)`

-- s 55(1): "If a surviving person who is wholly or substantially dependent on a deceased person has an entitlement under the
-- deceased person's will that does not become absolute until 30 days after his or her death, the deceased person's personal
-- representative may make a distribution for the maintenance, support or education of the surviving person before the 30
-- day period expires." (3): even with a Family Provision Act 1970 application pending. (4): deducted from the person's share.
-- (5): if the person does not survive 30 days, it is an administration expense. An "if" condition and a period the text
-- fixes: JUST FALSE outside them. JUST TRUE means the personal representative MAY pay, not that they must. "Before the 30
-- day period expires": a day up to and including the 30th day after the death (the day of death excluded, fork F6).
GIVEN `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 -- the personal representative may pay me maintenance now` `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the deceased` `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death` `the day of death` `today` MEANS
    IF     `I was wholly or substantially dependent on the deceased`
       AND `my entitlement under the will becomes absolute only 30 days after the death`
       AND `the days since the death` AT LEAST 0
       AND `the days since the death` AT MOST 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the days since the death` MEANS `the days from` `the day of death` `to` `today`
